operates through two segments, Retail Operations and Product Manufacturing. The company sells new and used recreational boats, including pleasure and fishing boats, mega-yachts, yachts, sport cruisers, motor yachts, e-power yachts, pontoon boats, ski boats, jet boats, and other recreational boats. It also offers marine parts and accessories comprising marine electronics; dock and anchoring products that include boat fenders, lines, and anchors; boat covers; trailer parts; water sport accessories, which comprise tubes, lines, wakeboards, and skis; engine parts; oils; lubricants; steering and control systems; corrosion control products and service products; high-performance accessories, including propellers and instruments; and a line of boating accessories, such as life jackets, inflatables, and water sports equipment. In addition, the company provides novelty items, such as shirts, caps, and license plates; marine engines and equipment; maintenance, repair, and slip and storage services; and boat or yacht brokerage services, as well as yacht charters and power catamarans. Further, it offers new or used boat finance services; arranges insurance coverage, including boat property, disability, undercoating, gel sealant, fabric protection, trailer tire and wheel protection, and casualty insurance coverage; and manufactures and sells sport yachts and yachts. Additionally, the company operates MarineMax vacations in Tortola and British Virgin Islands. It also markets and sells its products through offsite locations and print catalog. The company was incorporated in 1998 and is based in Oldsmar, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William Brett McGill | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["MarineMax, Inc.  (FL) is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.2B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $12M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9809342230695894},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"First Trust Capital Management L.P. Buys 636,478 Shares of MarineMax, Inc. $HZO","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/first-trust-capital-management-l-p-buys-636478-shares-of-marinemax-inc-hzo.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794562149.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.961,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Precision Trading with Marinemax Inc. (fl) (HZO) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Precision_Trading_with_Marinemax_Inc._fl_HZO_Risk_Zones_111126081202_1794445922.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794445922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MarineMax (HZO) Could Be 7% Overvalued On Fresh Earnings Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/marinemax-hzo-could-7-overvalued-091023537.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794129023.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MarineMax (HZO) Stock May Already Reflect Full Value Following Its $1.5B Buyout Deal","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/marinema